      "text_raw": "Sometimes a voltage refer-\nence is required which is\nnot referred to ground or\nsupply voltage. It is float-\ning. This necessitates a\nfull-differential opamp, as\nshown in this slide.\nThe principle is shown on\nthe left. Two pairs of sub-\nstrate pnp’s are used to gen-\nerate a double bandgap\nvoltage of about 2.4 V on\nthe right. For this purpose,\ntransistors Q1 and Q2 must\nbe biased by a PTAT cur-\nrent, which is not shown\nhere.",
      "text": "Sometimes a voltage reference is required which is not referred to ground or supply voltage. It is floating. This necessitates a full-differential opamp, as shown in this slide. The principle is shown on the left. Two pairs of substrate pnp’s are used to generate a double bandgap voltage of about 2.4 V on the right. For this purpose, transistors Q1 and Q2 must be biased by a PTAT current, which is not shown here."
